## Why is `aws configure` used?

`aws configure` is used to set up AWS CLI on your computer so you can connect to your AWS account and manage AWS resources using PowerShell or a terminal.

For example, instead of opening the AWS Console to check an EC2 instance, you can use a command like:

PowerShell

```
aws ec2 describe-instances
```

But first, AWS CLI needs to know which AWS account to use and how to authenticate. That's where `aws configure` comes in.

### 1. Run the command

Open PowerShell and type:

PowerShell

```
aws configure
```

It will ask you for four things:

```
AWS Access Key ID [None]:
AWS Secret Access Key [None]:
Default region name [None]:
Default output format [None]:
```

